<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><subtitle type="html">Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/rss</id><updated>2026-11-21T16:15:54Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Countries race to secure Cop31 deal</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d395b4164a9c101d5d95778fdb025a7739358c73482fe4295b6d3f58ca0b03e0</id><updated>2026-11-21T16:15:03Z</updated><published>2026-11-21T15:52:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/countries-race-to-secure-cop31-deal--bb7c67e08b7b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/countries-race-to-secure-cop31-deal" /><summary type="html">COP31 climate talks have overrun their schedule as countries race to agree on a new global climate deal, following criticism of an earlier draft that made no mention of fossil fuels. The EU has warned that the current proposal risks turning the summit into a “fossil fuel summit”, as negotiators work towards a revised, potentially final agreement expected later today. France 24 International affairs editor Jamie Smith-Maillet tells us more.</summary></entry><entry><title>New day of protests across France</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:78137d869ef5fa522a7083546f2e846c71224edcde277bac0050658ebb661662</id><updated>2026-11-21T16:15:06Z</updated><published>2026-11-21T15:50:52Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/new-day-of-protests-across-france--ebc936830291.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/new-day-of-protests-across-france" /><summary type="html">France faces a sixth consecutive Saturday of protests, with demonstrators taking to the streets to rally over the rising cost of living and the government's handling of weeks of social unrest ahead of next year's presidential election. France 24 journalist Antonia Kerrigan tells us more.</summary></entry><entry><title>Cargo ship runs aground off French coast</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:667c2e05b02ebbec98f3f2fdd432e99a300f0d24204f887f3e06eb905bb8a1c8</id><updated>2026-11-21T16:15:09Z</updated><published>2026-11-21T12:52:27Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/cargo-ship-runs-aground-off-french-coast--bad0e101e42b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/cargo-ship-runs-aground-off-french-coast" /><summary type="html">A Maltese-flagged cargo ship remains stranded off the coast of south-western France after running aground. French authorities are preparing an operation to prevent the vessel from capsizing and potentially causing pollution. The ship was not carrying any cargo, and all 19 crew members were safely evacuated by helicopter. Dan Quinlan reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Russia tests NATO’s eastern defences</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6ea155272a3452acb22be7bc91f48f0fdfa10a9c235029086ef3180d5b17afc7</id><updated>2026-11-21T16:15:12Z</updated><published>2026-11-21T12:50:35Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/russia-tests-nato-s-eastern-defences--177315271fc4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/russia-tests-nato-s-eastern-defences" /><summary type="html">Two Russian missiles and a suspected drone came down in Poland on Friday in what Prime Minister Donald Tusk said was likely an "intentional provocation" timed to coincide with European military exercises in the country for a possible postwar mission in Ukraine. Senior Lecturer in Conflict and Security at King's College in London, Domitilla Sagramoso, shares further insights.</summary></entry><entry><title>Thousands protest overs prices, education, military spending in France and Europe</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c3fac91da239d0b14823692796fd579bcfce0c600ed94bf500969b57da225d61</id><updated>2026-11-21T16:15:15Z</updated><published>2026-11-21T12:48:46Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/thousands-protest-overs-prices-education-military-spending-in-france-and-europe--ad0a7be34014.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/thousands-protest-overs-prices-education-military-spending-in-france-and-europe" /><summary type="html">France is bracing for a sixth consecutive Saturday of protests, with demonstrators expected to rally over the rising cost of living and the government's handling of weeks of social unrest ahead of next year's presidential election. France 24 journalist Antonia Kerrigan tells us the latest from Paris.</summary></entry><entry><title>Drone attack sets Russian cargo ship ablaze in Gulf of Finland</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c9cea905115eb17c59b6d985f3130dca606f5c275e73cfedd8c0ce331ae6e615</id><updated>2026-11-21T16:15:18Z</updated><published>2026-11-21T12:35:54Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261121-drone-attack-sets-russian-cargo-ship-ablaze-in-gulf-of-finland--c7c9c4110e34.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261121-drone-attack-sets-russian-cargo-ship-ablaze-in-gulf-of-finland" /><summary type="html">A Russian cargo ship caught fire after a drone strike in international waters in the Gulf of Finland on Saturday and later drifted into Finnish ⁠territorial waters, Finnish authorities said. Helsinki alerted NATO and imposed temporary restrictions in the area amid heightened tensions in the Baltic Sea.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Ethiopia: Tackling period poverty and stigma</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:76ef4b247e9c44ce1beb4b526f16a9bb9c8494f1c089f897e71883dab35a2142</id><updated>2026-11-21T16:15:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-21T12:22:44Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/ethiopia-tackling-period-poverty-and-stigma--4f0bded21225.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/ethiopia-tackling-period-poverty-and-stigma" /><summary type="html">In Ethiopia, entrepreneur Hanan Ahmed is tackling period poverty and the stigma surrounding menstruation. By producing affordable reusable sanitary pads and raising awareness in schools, she hopes to make menstrual health more accessible and help girls stay in class. Report by Awa Diouf &amp; Guillaume Gougeon.</summary></entry><entry><title>Ethiopia - Eritrea: Troops mobilise along the border</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9ca88f7450d29050d337417ee8dd85dc5011f90721fb261bcc7fc26d52f65c27</id><updated>2026-11-21T16:15:24Z</updated><published>2026-11-21T12:19:21Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/ethiopia-eritrea-troops-mobilise-along-the-border--34962d781eeb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/ethiopia-eritrea-troops-mobilise-along-the-border" /><summary type="html">More than 200 former Tigray People’s Liberation Front (TPLF) fighters surrendered to Ethiopia’s federal military Friday, state-affiliated media reported, amid escalating border tensions with neighboring Eritrea. France 24 correspondent Tom Canetti tells us the latest.</summary></entry><entry><title>Music strikes a chord at French protest</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4f5c20ca6a53dc8aa18d8042b1520b01979c520c03cf098f49d2994645e9937c</id><updated>2026-11-21T16:15:27Z</updated><published>2026-11-21T12:17:52Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/music-strikes-a-chord-at-french-protest--24382a03f5b2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/music-strikes-a-chord-at-french-protest" /><summary type="html">Throughout history, protest songs have brought people together across genres, rallying against war, racism, inequality and the establishment. Music is also playing a key role in the youth-led demonstrations here in France. Our reporters went to meet some of the musicians using their voices to express the protesters’ demands.</summary></entry><entry><title>'Accept cookies'? Russia collects data from swaths of unknowing Swedes</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a374252c8ac5e3b8ee97b39d4bfa8b9a67d1450b3dfd74cec1b8202a648b897b</id><updated>2026-11-21T16:15:30Z</updated><published>2026-11-21T10:55:32Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261121-accept-cookies-russia-collected-data-swaths-unknowing-swedes--a6892ead2cc3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261121-accept-cookies-russia-collected-data-swaths-unknowing-swedes" /><summary type="html">A Russian tech firm backed by an oligarch close to President Vladimir Putin has secretly been collecting data from hundreds of thousands – possibly millions – of Swedes, a newspaper investigation found. The revelation has rattled the Nordic nation, whose proximity to Russia and unusually open public records system make it particularly vulnerable to Moscow’s hybrid war tactics.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>'Unacceptable': EU chief condemns alleged Russian plot to kill US-Ukrainian citizen</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ef96677cfec4e884589537ae6e6c477352701d34486060ff4f46506de90046ac</id><updated>2026-11-21T16:15:33Z</updated><published>2026-11-21T10:32:36Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261121-unacceptable-eu-chief-condemns-alleged-russian-plot-to-kill-us-ukrainian-citizen--dca3e06988cd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261121-unacceptable-eu-chief-condemns-alleged-russian-plot-to-kill-us-ukrainian-citizen" /><summary type="html">European Commission President Ursula von der Leyen condemned an alleged Russian intelligence plot to assassinate a US-Ukrainian citizen in Denmark, vowing full solidarity with Copenhagen.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Was Vladimir Putin 'snubbed' by Xi Jinping? Viral handshake video is AI fake</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8cb82c1b5aaea05ecf72782c9ec993f65af7b9843b8571da68c472562f9dd8f5</id><updated>2026-11-21T16:15:36Z</updated><published>2026-11-21T10:16:44Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/truth-or-fake/20261121-was-vladimir-putin-snubbed-by-xi-jinping-viral-handshake-video-is-ai-fake--e3603b32fc23.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/truth-or-fake/20261121-was-vladimir-putin-snubbed-by-xi-jinping-viral-handshake-video-is-ai-fake" /><summary type="html">A viral video appearing to show China's Xi Jinping "snubbing" Vladimir Putin at the APEC summit has racked up millions of views, fuelling speculation about tensions between Beijing and Moscow. But the footage is fake. FRANCE 24 traced the original video to an earlier summit, where the two leaders did shake hands. The creator, who runs a satire account, admitted to manipulating the footage using Grok Imagine, an AI tool developed by Elon Musk's xAI, as Vedika Bahl explains.</summary><category term="Truth or Fake" /></entry><entry><title>Denmark accuses Russia of assassination plot, expels diplomat</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3889f4040f8af26acdae4ebc1f82098663b73022a20c66f4bc61138f76ca059f</id><updated>2026-11-21T16:15:39Z</updated><published>2026-11-21T09:51:01Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/denmark-accuses-russia-of-assassination-plot-expels-diplomat--a5fea2e1ca7c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/denmark-accuses-russia-of-assassination-plot-expels-diplomat" /><summary type="html">Denmark has accused Moscow of being behind a failed assassination attempt targeting a Ukrainian-American rapper in Copenhagen, further escalating tensions between Europe and Russia. In response, Danish authorities have ordered the expulsion of a Russian diplomat and announced tighter restrictions on visas for Russian tourists. Yuka Royer reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Houthis launch strikes on Saudi Arabia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4cf7cd57a77b0c5d1c9edbeb06dbbf84b51981ceb66bd1accdbef4a11e933c5f</id><updated>2026-11-21T16:15:42Z</updated><published>2026-11-21T09:49:44Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/houthis-launch-strikes-on-saudi-arabia--258e24a13d6a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/houthis-launch-strikes-on-saudi-arabia" /><summary type="html">Iran-backed Houthi rebels in Yemen continue to exchange strikes with the Saudi-led coalition. The coalition said it intercepted and destroyed three ballistic missiles fired towards Riyadh early on Saturday. It marks the second Houthi attack on the Saudi capital in recent days, following Saudi-led strikes on Houthi targets in Yemen. Yuka Royer has the latest.</summary></entry><entry><title>Russian projectiles hit Poland as NATO tensions rise</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c6d2ab76f4f375abac9449c29953c39464bef7f0aab63a954a55f62b6f45d1b8</id><updated>2026-11-21T16:15:45Z</updated><published>2026-11-21T09:47:05Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/russian-projectiles-hit-poland-as-nato-tensions-rise--b3f05afbc166.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/russian-projectiles-hit-poland-as-nato-tensions-rise" /><summary type="html">Three Russian projectiles came down in Poland on Friday, prompting NATO to condemn what it called a grave violation of Polish airspace. A suspected jet-powered drone and a missile struck separate locations near the Ukrainian border, while another missile crashed just 35 kilometres from an area where European troops are taking part in military exercises. Meanwhile, troops from eight NATO countries are conducting drills in neighbouring Lithuania. With US-led peace talks yet to make a breakthrough, tensions between Europe and Russia remain high. Peter O’Brien reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Nations League: France to face Spain in quarter-finals, England to take on Norway</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d8b951eaa53458ca5e3f912dea8a9623e8a155bd2fff36cef7cb3877285a7d29</id><updated>2026-11-21T16:15:48Z</updated><published>2026-11-21T09:46:43Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/sports/20261121-nations-league-france-to-face-spain-in-quarter-finals-england-to-take-on-norway--f62a769b042d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/sports/20261121-nations-league-france-to-face-spain-in-quarter-finals-england-to-take-on-norway" /><summary type="html">A chance for revenge. Beaten by Spain in the World Cup semi-finals last July, France will meet La Roja again in the Nations League quarter-finals next March.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>EU, UK reach reset deal after Brexit</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8ff6a3cb447cb3637fae77623bef13ba7ac528e86fdf262032ffdc9567c69e8d</id><updated>2026-11-21T16:15:51Z</updated><published>2026-11-21T09:43:42Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/eu-uk-reach-reset-deal-after-brexit--3244a7b00c69.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/eu-uk-reach-reset-deal-after-brexit" /><summary type="html">The UK and the EU signed three agreements on Friday at a summit in Brussels, marking a new effort to reset post-Brexit relations. The deals aim to reduce red tape for food exports, link emissions trading schemes and allow tens of thousands of young people to live and work more freely across the Channel. Prime Minister Andy Burnham has called Brexit an “obvious failure” to deliver on its promises and wants to deepen ties with the EU, a position criticised by veteran Brexiteer Nigel Farage, who has warned of a political backlash. Daniel Quinlan has this story.</summary></entry><entry><title>Live: Demonstrators rally across France for sixth consecutive Saturday of protests</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0453f1f9531badec4fb44f10a63c82a8e6330af256c92fe4f53aa97ff19e821f</id><updated>2026-11-21T16:15:54Z</updated><published>2026-11-21T08:29:53Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/france/20261121-live-france-braces-for-fresh-protests-as-social-unrest-enters-sixth-week--ba7b313f65f2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france/20261121-live-france-braces-for-fresh-protests-as-social-unrest-enters-sixth-week" /><summary type="html">France faces a sixth consecutive Saturday of protests, with demonstrators taking to the streets to rally over the rising cost of living and the government's handling of weeks of social unrest ahead of next year's presidential election. Follow our liveblog for the latest developments.</summary><category term="France" /></entry><entry><title>US Agriculture Department and FBI hit by cyberattacks, media report</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2eb7941d5d5cda3d6f45c4b332ea9b9a7e7a9eba1ef15cb7bbb04a2fb0038136</id><updated>2026-11-21T16:14:02Z</updated><published>2026-11-21T07:01:04Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261121-us-agriculture-department-fbi-hit-by-cyberattacks-media-report--56cdf33f7140.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261121-us-agriculture-department-fbi-hit-by-cyberattacks-media-report" /><summary type="html">Hackers breached systerms at the US Agriculture Department and the FBI, US media reported, amid a recent wave of major technology disruptions across the country.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>House of Cards: America's enemies "no longer fear it, its allies no longer trust it'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6c2a39e0652484682cdfdbb4dcbff1ad007ed2c2d88bcb183cb2bce19614a507</id><updated>2026-11-21T16:14:02Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T22:13:21Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261120-house-of-cards-america-s-enemies-no-longer-fear-it-its-allies-no-longer-trust-it--88bb89bac749.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261120-house-of-cards-america-s-enemies-no-longer-fear-it-its-allies-no-longer-trust-it" /><summary type="html">The Economist's deputy editor Tom Standage joins us for a futuristic retrospective, taking us back to the future as we spotlight "The World Ahead 2027". We begin with the "leader of the free world", the FIFA Peace Prize recipient presiding over an America under the "Donroe Doctrine": "Its enemies no longer fear it and its allies no longer trust it in the way they did before."</summary><category term="Spotlight" /></entry><entry><title>Paris police officers sentenced to prison over 2020 beating of Black man</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:93f429e74d27c61966eb33397aac8fa55e8cf2bb369123202a2caf28faf6dcc2</id><updated>2026-11-21T16:14:02Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T22:04:45Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/france/20261120-paris-police-officers-sentenced-to-prison-over-2020-beating-of-black-man-michel-zecler--0c3d3dca1060.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france/20261120-paris-police-officers-sentenced-to-prison-over-2020-beating-of-black-man-michel-zecler" /><summary type="html">A Paris court on Friday sentenced three policemen to serve time over the 2020 beating of Black music producer Michel Zecler, a rare such ruling. The assault, which was captured on camera, sparked nationwide outrage and renewed scrutiny of police violence and racism in France.</summary><category term="France" /></entry><entry><title>Guinea bans Burkina Faso broadcaster, escalating diplomatic tensions</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3f0cebd1def97cb8db770c9f580b9e2bfb48d54e8d4607ab8bb16c7b74a206bc</id><updated>2026-11-21T16:14:02Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T21:53:35Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/eye-on-africa/20261120-guinea-bans-burkina-faso-broadcaster-escalating-diplomatic-tensions--8233ee4e0a4a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/eye-on-africa/20261120-guinea-bans-burkina-faso-broadcaster-escalating-diplomatic-tensions" /><summary type="html">Tensions rise between Guinea and Burkina Faso after Conakry bans Burkinabe broadcaster RTB, amid a diplomatic dispute over gold miners and a caricature of President Mamadi Doumbouya. Meanwhile, fighting erupts between Congolese forces and the Rwanda-backed FRN group in eastern DR Congo, despite peace commitments. Finally, in Ethiopia, one entrepreneur is tackling period poverty by breaking menstrual stigma and making reusable sanitary pads more accessible.</summary><category term="Eye on Africa" /></entry><entry><title>'Licence to kill': France adopts law presuming 'legitimate' self-defence in police shootings</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1f59740e095692817596ef3c0c9d963e6136794fee6ed53812daf460c6d32d25</id><updated>2026-11-21T16:14:02Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T21:17:59Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/france/20261120-licence-to-kill-french-parliament-adopts-police-shootings-law-slammed-activists--f621fb1622a7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france/20261120-licence-to-kill-french-parliament-adopts-police-shootings-law-slammed-activists" /><summary type="html">French senators gave final approval on Friday to controversial legislation granting police officers a presumption of legitimate self-defence when using firearms, fulfilling a long-standing demand of the far right even as weeks of student-led protests have thrust the issue of police brutality back into the spotlight. Left-wing lawmakers have vowed to challenge the bill.</summary><category term="France" /></entry><entry><title>'Friends' But Who Benefits? Notes from an Historic Summit, Myanmar's Genocide Ruling, Time to 'Bre-join' the EU?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6e1ea67686bb9a37768ae64de7dfc4b87a64b8421bf52668829575f9f685bcf1</id><updated>2026-11-21T16:14:02Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T19:42:58Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-world-this-week/20261120-friends-but-who-benefits-notes-from-an-historic-summit-myanmar-s-genocide-ruling-time-to-br--18c7cf7590a8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-world-this-week/20261120-friends-but-who-benefits-notes-from-an-historic-summit-myanmar-s-genocide-ruling-time-to-bre-join-the-eu" /><summary type="html">Welcome to the World This Week with Gavin Lee. You give us 45 minutes, we'll give you 7 days worth of crystal clear analysis. As ever, alongside a handpicked panel of four distinguished foreign correspondents.</summary><category term="The World This Week" /></entry></feed>
